# Monitoring Stack Application
# Deploys: Prometheus, Grafana, Alertmanager, Jaeger
---
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: monitoring
  namespace: argocd
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: monitoring
    app.kubernetes.io/part-of: enclii
  finalizers:
    - resources-finalizer.argocd.argoproj.io
spec:
  project: default

  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/madfam-org/enclii.git
    targetRevision: main
    path: infra/k8s/production/monitoring

  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: monitoring

  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      prune: true
      selfHeal: true
    syncOptions:
      - CreateNamespace=true
      - ServerSideApply=true

  # NO ignoreDifferences.
  #
  # This app used to exempt ConfigMap/prometheus-config `/data/prometheus.yml`
  # from the diff, on the stated premise that it "may have scrape targets added
  # dynamically". Nothing does that: Prometheus discovers targets through
  # kubernetes_sd_configs, and the config file itself is static. The premise was
  # defensive rather than observed, and it was added in the original GitOps
  # foundation commit.
  #
  # The cost was that the scrape config became permanently un-deployable. Argo
  # reported `Synced` while ignoring every change to the one key that matters,
  # so the live ConfigMap sat at whatever was last applied by hand — its own
  # managedFields show argocd-controller last writing it 2026-05-06, three
  # months before this line was removed, while the neighbouring
  # prometheus-rules ConfigMap (not exempted) updated the same day it changed.
  #
  # That is how the pushgateway went 96 days unscraped: adding the job to git
  # would not have helped, because git had no authority over this file. Every
  # metric pushed by the CronJob monitors — argo_main_parity_*, the whole
  # deploy-pipeline-monitor family — went to a gateway Prometheus never read,
  # and every alert built on them was dead on arrival. Found 2026-08-11.
  #
  # If a future change genuinely needs a runtime-mutated scrape config, scope
  # the exemption to that key and say what writes it — never to the whole file,
  # and never without a control that proves the ignored field still matches
  # intent.
